{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1310297-mages-who-live-thousands-of-years-old","id":1310297,"title":"Mages who live thousands of years old?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-06T09:05:34-07:00","id":1310297,"title":"Mages who live thousands of years old?","content":"Sorry I have a typo in topic...<br /> <br /> So, I want to design a Meths-old mage because of my friend(Yeah...), and he MUST LIVE FOR thousands of years, not be in some special conditions like buried in a tomb(!). Did anyone think about this kind of characters? What do you think of it?<br /> <br /> You can share your suggestions, concepts and characters.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Uh, my opinion:<br /> <br /> Of course I recall and , which has settings applying to this. And some Canon NPCs.<br /> <br /> 1. First I think about prolonging life(including dealing with Paradox). He can't just live with those two immortality Rotes, so he should have more effective methods. Archspheres is simple, Lichdom also works but it is very difficult and dangerous and has many traps. Paradox is another problem, he will accumulate ridiculous Permandox if we use rules in H:tSoH, so it is more likely that he will live in Umbra forever.<br /> <br /> 2. Second I think about rules for Meths in VtM to specify him. after all they have much in common. So I recall and some Elder books.<br /> <br /> 3. Third I check Canon statted NPCs out, but I find they all have some special ideas:<br /> <br /> Medea is a Greek Mythology figures.<br /> <br /> Al-aswad has a very &quot;mystical&quot; background which can't be referred to simply, Aswadims too.<br /> <br /> Nesna Nethshrac is the first liche, and be buried in tomb for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> These are mages who live thousands of years I can remember...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 05-08-2019, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T09:32:21-07:00","id":1310302,"title":"","content":"Take the unaging merit and invent a good reason for it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T09:38:45-07:00","id":1310304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1310297-mages-who-live-thousands-of-years-old?p=1310302#post1310302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the unaging merit and invent a good reason for it</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh what's your good reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 05-06-2019, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T10:19:46-07:00","id":1310313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1310297-mages-who-live-thousands-of-years-old?p=1310304#post1310304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh what's your good reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>That will depend on the character background history. Being a technomancer he might use nano particles that rebuild cells or stop the oxidation. <br /> Maybe he drunk from a fountain of youth. Or just used a powerful Life ritual (or found someone to do it).<br /> Maybe he gathered all 7 dragonballs and asked for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T10:46:49-07:00","id":1310318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1310297-mages-who-live-thousands-of-years-old?p=1310313#post1310313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That will depend on the character background history. Being a technomancer he might use nano particles that rebuild cells or stop the oxidation. <br /> Maybe he drunk from a fountain of youth. Or just used a powerful Life ritual (or found someone to do it).<br /> Maybe he gathered all 7 dragonballs and asked for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>...So can you give me more reasonable details about background? And man are you serious? I have admitted I have a careless typo in topic and my English isn't good. Yeah eventually rules and settings are all selectable for players, but it is meaningless if you are very very fantastic and far from them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 05-06-2019, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T11:18:34-07:00","id":1310324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1310297-mages-who-live-thousands-of-years-old?p=1310318#post1310318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...So can you give me more reasonable details about background? And man are you serious? I have admitted I have a careless typo in topic and my English isn't good. Yeah eventually rules and settings are all selectable for players, but it is meaningless if you are very very fantastic and far from them...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage can be very very fantastic.<br /> I'd say that posting his background dots, tradition and style (mystic/techno) is a good start.<br /> <br /> Any of my options interested you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T11:57:28-07:00","id":1310334,"title":"","content":"As <i>Lord Revan</i> said. Mages are fantastic like that, and that's why they have loads of weird Merits. Hence it's more a matter of what's flavorful for the character (and the story) than anything established:<br /> <br /> Maybe the mage found some secret in the ancient times where magick was more common and the barriers between worlds were weaker, like the protag of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Immortal_(short_story)\" target=\"_blank\">The Immortal </a><br /> <br /> Maybe the character has the blessing (or suffers the curse) of a very &quot;high&quot; power like the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wandering_Jew\" target=\"_blank\">Wandering Jew</a><br /> <br /> (note that both these characters are different takes on the same legend of Cartaphilus / Joseph of Arimathea /etc...Ha, immortals. Your character probably has many names too. Of course, your character it's not trully immortal, but *just* unaging...however, that difference it's moot if he never died)<br /> <br /> If Mummy hadn't taken that seat already, he could be one of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eight_Immortals\" target=\"_blank\">Eight Immortals</a>.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the mage it's a living construct made by Hephaestus imperishable bronze, and that's why he doesn't age. One forgets gods sometimes do stuff<br /> <br /> Being a Nephilim heir of a god of longevity (or perhaps of death) sounds like a good reason.<br /> <br /> I once built a character that was a chess loving old man that experienced death at his Awakening (like some Euthanatos do) as his heart stopped (he was very old and it was his time). He experienced his Avatar as Death (The Grim Reaper) and, <i>of course</i>, he <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ChessWithDeath\" target=\"_blank\">played chess with Death</a>. He won (kinda...the idea was more complicated) and now he's Unaging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-06-2019, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T12:01:33-07:00","id":1310336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1310297-mages-who-live-thousands-of-years-old?p=1310304#post1310304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh what's your good reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>If he is an antediluvean, then he may have eaten from the Tree of Life (or whatever the culturally appropriate counterpart would be).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T20:01:39-07:00","id":1310459,"title":"","content":"The Unaging Merit permits cheap access to what is, in-universe, a very rare condition, because that state is ultimately not actually that valuable or important to the timeline of an individual game.<br /> <br /> Life can just extend someone's lifespan, though usually this is presented as requiring greater and greater amounts of rarefied reagents or Tass to maintain.<br /> <br /> Mind and Matter can invest the mage's consciousness in a more durable vessel, such as a marble or brass body.<br /> <br /> Mind and Life could allow a mage to be &quot;reborn&quot; through one of their descendants. I've had an NPC antagonist in our game use a method akin to this - they used Life, Mind, and Prime to create a very complicated living Wonder, a child with incredible physical and mental aptitudes, and suspended a Time/Entropy/Mind effect to possess the body after the kid had grown to adulthood.<br /> <br /> What if the mage isn't immortal, but is using a very sophisticated Time effect? They don't live forever, exactly, but they're gliding across the surface of their own timeline - the mage only really exists when he's doing something significant, and so only really ages a couple of hours each year.<br /> <br /> More esoteric, imagine a Mind/Entropy/Time/Prime effect tied to the Destiny Merit. The mage no longer exists as a distinct individual, but has a potent Destiny attached to their Avatar and an effect which causes their subsequent incarnations to exhibit the mage's personality and memories when they're involved in that Destiny. In other words, the mage &quot;Steve&quot; has technically died, but anyone with Steve's Avatar temporarily turns into Steve when they run into one of Steve's old acquaintances or enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T03:22:09-07:00","id":1310705,"title":"","content":"A good justification for Unaging could be some cosmic curse. Not Caine level, but some powerful god or spirit cursed the character (via an intermediary, some angel or lesser spirit) so that they'd be stuck with something bad until they repented for the sin. However a weird side-effect of that, which doesn't seem like a big deal to the immortal spirits, is that their aging is put on hold until the curse resolves itself. Naturally this means you take some flaws to represent the downside of the curse that they need to live with.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, they could be unaging because they found one of the old Hermetic Youth Formulae, and actually managed to get it to work. People agree that it shouldn't have worked, since powers like that have faded away with the end of the mystic era, but it did work in your case. It's just a shame that you can't replicate that success, no matter how hard you try, since if you could you'd be one of the most powerful Hermetics. Many powerful mages fear death, and would do a lot to get their hands on a safe agelessness potion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T04:06:57-07:00","id":1310709,"title":"","content":"Something tangential but possibly important is that Mages' immortality doesn't have to come with the same memory benefits as the Kindred (least as of 5e). An antedeluvian mage could just forget where they came from or who they are. I mean, by default a mage that old has more or less staled in their Ascension, memory lose and confusion would kinda go with that quite well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T04:11:13-07:00","id":1310710,"title":"","content":"Uh I appreciate you everybody's ideas about my first tip very much. But does anyone have more ideas about OTHER things? How does he extend his life when he is just a normal mage, not a Chosen or Gifted one(although guys in Canon are all like this)?What's your own rules or experience of creating this kind of guys? What's your stats you have made? Or can anyone remember more Canon NPCs like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 05-08-2019, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T04:30:25-07:00","id":1310716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1310297-mages-who-live-thousands-of-years-old?p=1310710#post1310710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does he extend his life when he is just a normal mage, not a Chosen or Gifted one?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd help if you identified what you don't like about the ways suggested. It seems like you're looking for something specific but you haven't said what exactly.<br /> <br /> Also, is this an NPC or a PC?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T04:33:04-07:00","id":1310717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1310297-mages-who-live-thousands-of-years-old?p=1310709#post1310709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something tangential but possibly important is that Mages' immortality doesn't have to come with the same memory benefits as the Kindred (least as of 5e). An antedeluvian mage could just forget where they came from or who they are. I mean, by default a mage that old has more or less staled in their Ascension, memory lose and confusion would kinda go with that quite well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, reasons? If you choose to reborn this may become true.<br /> And btw, I haven't have a close reading on VtM 5E, does anything about Really ancient vampires change? Like Advanced Disciplines or Traits? In my memory this is also a standard book, but stats given to mortal hunters are... overrated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 05-08-2019, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T04:50:43-07:00","id":1310720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1310297-mages-who-live-thousands-of-years-old?p=1310716#post1310716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'd help if you identified what you don't like about the ways suggested. It seems like you're looking for something specific but you haven't said what exactly.<br /> <br /> Also, is this an NPC or a PC?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I like all suggestions, I just want to steer more to all-round things...<br /> Five Eyes gives several good ways to a normal mage.<br /> <br /> Both NPC and PC.<br /> <br /> Okay sorry I haven't said exactly.<br /> I mean if he isn't a gifted one, just a normal mage who must make an effort to get anything he want, what should he do to prolong his life? After all Unaging Merit is a simple way...<br /> <br /> And what's your understanding about this kind of mage? Like, what status or background should he have? How does he live? What's his influence about Ascension War or other lesser mages?<br /> <br /> If you really want to create this kind of NPCs, which book will you refer to? How will you add dots on his Sheets","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T05:00:14-07:00","id":1310721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1310297-mages-who-live-thousands-of-years-old?p=1310717#post1310717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, why?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the underlying idea of the setting. I mean, you seem to have read Master of the Art, it's pretty explicit. You don't need thousands of years to reach ascension; so if your character is thousands of years old then something has gone wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And btw, I haven't have a close reading on VtM 5E, does anything about Really ancient vampires change? </div> </div> </div>I haven't read it that closely either. I just picked up a line where it makes the explicit point that vampires have a supernaturally good memory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T05:08:39-07:00","id":1310722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1310297-mages-who-live-thousands-of-years-old?p=1310721#post1310721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the underlying idea of the setting. I mean, you seem to have read Master of the Art, it's pretty explicit. You don't need thousands of years to reach ascension; so if your character is thousands of years old then something has gone wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will re-read it, maybe I have a bad memory.<br /> <br /> Uh but if he is an exception? Like Larth became a Liche in order to defend his country forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 05-08-2019, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113"